    "title": "Conflict de-escalation pause protocol",
    "category": "Practical · Emergency · Expansion",
    "subcategory": "Conflict · Deescalation",
    "summary": "Separate immediate safety from the disputed issue, lower voices, reduce the audience, identify needs, and appoint a neutral timekeeper.",
    "content": "Pause the decision when fatigue, weapons, intoxication, threats, or loss of control are present and move to safety. Do not surround, shame, touch, corner, or threaten a distressed person.",
